<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">toxĭcum</span></b> , i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοξικόν;</span> orig., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a poison in which
				arrows were dipped</i>, Caecil. and Afran. ap. <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				355</span></i> Müll.; <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 4,
				7, 11</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 10, 20, § 51</span></i>.
			— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>poison</i>, in
			gen. (syn. venenum); sing., <i><span class="en">Plaut. Merc.
				2, 4, 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miscere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 17, 61</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Ner. 35</span></i>. — <i>Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bibere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					1, 5, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 2, 2, 64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 9,
			820</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 1, 19, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 10,
			18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
